+# Changes — round 0
+
+## What changed
+
+- `src/truncate.mjs` (new): exports `truncate(text, max)`. Text of at most
+  `max` characters is returned unchanged; longer text is cut to `max - 1`
+  characters and finished with a single "…" (U+2026), so the result is exactly
+  `max` characters long. Whitespace is neither trimmed nor collapsed. A `text`
+  that is not a string throws a `TypeError` (checked first); a `max` that is not
+  a positive integer (`Number.isInteger(max) && max >= 1`) throws a `RangeError`,
+  which refuses `0`, `-1`, `2.5`, `"3"`, `NaN`, `Infinity`, `null`, `undefined`
+  and `true`. Characters are counted with `.length`, as `padStart` does.
+- `tests/truncate.test.mjs` (new): covers unchanged text, the boundary at
+  exactly `max`, cutting to exactly `max`, the U+2026 ellipsis (not three dots),
+  `max` of 1, whitespace handling, and every refused value above.
+- `CHANGELOG.md`: added the `truncate` line under `## Unreleased`.
+
+## Findings addressed
